            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "In theory we could also implement this per uid, but I'm not sure that's worth it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 29,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Code golf/nitpick\n\nstatic uint8_t instanceId = 0xFF;\ninstanceId++;\ninstanceId &= ocp::accelerator_management::instanceIdBitMask;\nreturn instanceId;\n\n\n\nThe above is slightly easier to read, and gets the same result without an extra variable or a compound statement.  Change if you want."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuVoltageSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 116,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Should this be done in the mctp layer?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuVoltageSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 116,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "I went back and forth on that. It could be. I don't have a strong opinion either way. It would be cleaner than requiring an extra (needless) fn parameter and I can't think of a reason why it shouldn't be in the mctp layer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuVoltageSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 116,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "My thinking is that because it's global to the application/mctp connection, there's no value other than getNextIid() that an api could put that would make this correct."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuVoltageSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 116,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/82594 does it in the MCTP layer. I don't think we need both the patches. My vote is to do it in the MCTP layer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuVoltageSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 116,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/82594 is far more complicated than what this patch is proposing, and also hasn't been responded to in a month.\n\nI'd advocate for a merge of the two.  The simple in-memory increasing uuid being done in the mctp layer."
                }
            ],
